{"reference":"1 Samuel 12","book":"1 Samuel","chapter":12,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"Kingship and accountability","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"The chapter presents the king as both chosen by the people and set over them by the LORD. Its central warning is that monarchy does not replace Israel's obligation to fear, serve, and obey the LORD: the king and the people stand under the same demand for faithfulness.","verse_refs":["1 Samuel 12:1-25"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_1_samuel_012_35551cd027aaa3343c4481e9"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]},{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"The larger movement of First Samuel","blocks":[{"id":"block_2","text":"This chapter belongs to a larger story that moves from the failure of Eli's priestly house, through Samuel's prophetic leadership, to Saul's kingship and its rejection, before turning to David's rise and Saul's death. Samuel's address marks a major transition within that wider movement.","verse_refs":["1 Samuel 1","1 Samuel 10:1-27","1 Samuel 11:1-15","1 Samuel 13:1-23","1 Samuel 14:1-52","1 Samuel 15:1-35","1 Samuel 16:1-23","1 Samuel 17:1-58","1 Samuel 18:1-30","1 Samuel 19:1-24","1 Samuel 20:1-42","1 Samuel 21:1-15","1 Samuel 22:1-23","1 Samuel 23:1-29","1 Samuel 24:1-22","1 Samuel 25:1-44","1 Samuel 26:1-25","1 Samuel 27:1-12","1 Samuel 28:1-25","1 Samuel 29:1-11","1 Samuel 2:1-36","1 Samuel 30:1-31","1 Samuel 31:1-13","1 Samuel 3:1-21","1 Samuel 4:1-22","1 Samuel 5:1-12","1 Samuel 6:1-21","1 Samuel 7:1-17","1 Samuel 8:1-22","1 Samuel 9:1-27"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_1_samuel_012_9382fce8e8fb514da1dca4b3"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"fact"},{"id":"block_3","text":"Across 1 Samuel 8-12, the account holds together severe criticism of Israel's request for a king and the positive divine selection and empowerment of Saul. On this reading, kingship is neither treated as simply good nor simply evil; it is permitted, yet remains accountable within Israel's covenant life.","verse_refs":["1 Samuel 10:1-27","1 Samuel 11:1-15","1 Samuel 8","1 Samuel 9:1-27"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_1_samuel_012_2d05a3cc77d988f7812bdb06"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}